= Tutored Lessons
Apache Incubator PMC
2026-08-22
:jbake-type: guide
:jbake-status: published
:idprefix:
:toc:
:imagesdir: ../images/

== Tutored Lessons

Each lesson is an interactive session with an AI tutor rather than a document
to read. You paste the lesson into a chat model, and it teaches you one idea at
a time, sets exercises, waits for your answer before giving its own, and
finishes with a self-check.

The lessons are written and fact-checked against ASF policy, the Incubator's
guides and the Incubator wiki, and they are explicit about which of those a
given statement comes from.

== How to run one

. Click *Copy prompt* next to the lesson you want.
. Open any capable chat model.
. Paste the prompt as the first message, or into a system prompt field if the
tool has one.
. Say hello. The tutor takes it from there.

Nothing is installed and nothing is recorded. If you prefer, *View* opens the
plain text so you can read it first or copy it by hand.

== Foundations

Start here. These three are the prerequisite for everything below, and they
assume no prior knowledge of the ASF.

[cols="1,5,2",options="header"]
|===
| # | Lesson | Prompt

| 1
| *What the Incubator is, and whether you want it* +
What a podling is, what a project hands over and gets back, who does what, and
whether a community is ready to propose.
| link:lessons/lesson-01.md[View] +
  link:lessons/lesson-01.md[Copy prompt, role="copy-lesson"]

| 2
| *The Apache Way, in practice* +
Consensus, merit, community over code, transparency and independence, and how to
tell whether a decision was made the Apache way.
| link:lessons/lesson-02.md[View] +
  link:lessons/lesson-02.md[Copy prompt, role="copy-lesson"]

| 3
| *Working in public: lists, tone, culture, time zones* +
Why messages read as rude when nobody meant it, choosing the right channel,
working across time zones, and what the code of conduct asks.
| link:lessons/lesson-03.md[View] +
  link:lessons/lesson-03.md[Copy prompt, role="copy-lesson"]
|===

== Podling startup and the PPMC

For people running a podling day to day. These five can be taken in any order.

[cols="1,5,2",options="header"]
|===
| # | Lesson | Prompt

| 4
| *From proposal to podling* +
The path from idea to podling: what a champion does, what a proposal has to
establish, credible initial committers, and honest known risks.
| link:lessons/lesson-04.md[View] +
  link:lessons/lesson-04.md[Copy prompt, role="copy-lesson"]

| 5
| *Getting set up with Infra* +
What Infra does and what the project does, choosing between self-serve, a ticket
and Whimsy, and writing a request that needs no round trip.
| link:lessons/lesson-05.md[View] +
  link:lessons/lesson-05.md[Copy prompt, role="copy-lesson"]

| 6
| *How decisions get made: lazy consensus, votes, vetoes* +
When something needs no vote, consensus or a formal vote, who is binding, the
two-stage release vote, and what makes a veto valid.
| link:lessons/lesson-06.md[View] +
  link:lessons/lesson-06.md[Copy prompt, role="copy-lesson"]

| 7
| *Growing committers and the PPMC* +
What committers and PPMC members can and cannot do, running each process end to
end, who to invite, and the awkward cases.
| link:lessons/lesson-07.md[View] +
  link:lessons/lesson-07.md[Copy prompt, role="copy-lesson"]

| 8
| *Writing a report the IPMC can use* +
Who reads a podling report and what they look for, what belongs in each section,
reporting a bad month honestly, and the submission mechanics.
| link:lessons/lesson-08.md[View] +
  link:lessons/lesson-08.md[Copy prompt, role="copy-lesson"]
|===

== If you use Claude

The same eight lessons are packaged as a Claude skill, which saves the pasting.
Install it once, then `/incubator-lesson list` shows the catalogue and
`/incubator-lesson 6` starts that lesson. The lesson text in the skill is copied
from the same files this page publishes, so both routes run the same tutor.

Build it from a checkout with `python3 tools/ai-tutor/build-skill.py`, then
upload the packaged skill in your Claude settings.

== A caution

These are teaching prompts, not policy. Where a lesson and an ASF policy page
disagree, the policy page is correct. Models also make mistakes, so if you need
a definitive answer for a real decision, ask your mentors or
link:https://lists.apache.org/list.html?general@incubator.apache.org[general@incubator.apache.org].

Corrections are welcome on that list. The lessons live in
link:https://github.com/apache/incubator/tree/master/tools/ai-tutor[tools/ai-tutor]
in the website repository.

++++
<script>
(function () {
  function flash(el, text) {
    var original = el.textContent;
    el.textContent = text;
    setTimeout(function () { el.textContent = original; }, 2000);
  }
  document.addEventListener('click', function (event) {
    var link = event.target.closest ? event.target.closest('a.copy-lesson') : null;
    if (!link) { return; }
    event.preventDefault();
    var url = link.getAttribute('href');
    fetch(url).then(function (response) {
      if (!response.ok) { throw new Error(response.status); }
      return response.text();
    }).then(function (text) {
      return navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
    }).then(function () {
      flash(link, 'Copied');
    }).catch(function () {
      // Clipboard access can be blocked, and older browsers lack it entirely.
      // Send the reader to the file rather than leaving them with nothing.
      window.location.href = url;
    });
  });
})();
</script>
++++
